    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11507" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crĕātrix</span></b> ,
			īcis, f.
		creator, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>she who brings forth</i> or <i>produces, a mother</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">natura rerum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr. 1, 630 al.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mea, patria (with genetrix),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					63, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diva (of a mother),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 8, 534</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Alexandri Magni, Olympias,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aur.
					Vict. Epit. 40</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dira bellorum (tellus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					15, 184</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ambros. Fid. 4, 30, 3</span></i>.</div>
